; Close the first object
;
; Verb handler of command 12, "close", in the verb tables of doors, chests and
; the like (and the shared close of #R$A67E and #R$A761). When the object is not
; open it says "<object> is closed" (state id 5, see #R$A16C); otherwise it
; clears the open flag (bit 5 of the flags).
; .
; Nothing changes unless the command is really performed (CommitOrAbort).
;
; Noun1Record Record of the object to close
@label=CloseObject
c$9138 LD IX,($B708)     ;
 $913C CALL $A5CA        ; open?
 $913F JP Z,$A16C        ; no: "<it> is closed"
 $9142 CALL $9D44        ; abandon unless performing
@label=CloseObject_Clear
@isub=RES FLAG_ACTIVE,(IX+$07)
 $9145 RES 5,(IX+$07)    ; no longer open
 $9149 RET               ;
